    "body": "Venus gains a standalone local operator/executor for qualified signed releases, host-file PostgreSQL backups, and compatible recovery that preserves protected deletion/catalog ledgers. The PR also includes the already accepted P05 baseline; P07 is outside scope.\n\nA published OCI image can have a Docker Desktop native ID different from its config digest. Installation now verifies actual config bytes and source/version labels separately, binds the verified native ID, and preserves that distinction through cache-absent offline archive recovery. No consumer or operator daemon privileges are added.\n\nBy owner decision U-021 / ADR-033, automatic CI has five required checks: quality, container-smoke, p02-integration, p03-integration, and p06-release-integration. The four unchanged large P03 statistics suites are a separate optional manual workflow. Strict checks and the other main protection settings are preserved.\n\nValidation: clean source9434257/core d44f9f1f/1951files; 34 Linux unit tests passed, 18 actual Docker controls passed including nine SIGKILL phases and genuine cache-absent registry-off image restore; two independent pre-sign05 reviews passed. Current PR head4897538d uses the same implementation bytes and is running its five required CI checks. The source-bound release gate and docs check passed.\n\nThe owner-requested unsigned preview0.0.0 is published and publicly pullable at ghcr.io/psewdon1m/venus@sha256:0653678d4cbc920daf684355ddde5c7006d04aa89f950e2697e7fe4a5b7f4b3e (source195e2302). Qualified venus-v0.0.1 still requires exact main/tag, actual signed assets and exact published image verification. Production/DNS/TLS/device checks are not local PASS.\n",
